section: codegen
synopsis: The Cmm sinking pass no longer treats ``touch#``, arithmetic
  helpers such as ``quotRemInt#`` and ``timesWord2#``, bit operations, or
  libm calls as clobbering memory, so a load preceding one of them can be
  folded into the instruction that uses it, as in ``ByteString`` indexing.
